<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
	<!--
		Data Protection.

		The whole app container is created with the Complete protection class, so
		diary text, attachments cached by WebKit and the Supabase session token
		in WKWebView localStorage are unreadable while the device is locked. This
		is the iOS counterpart of android:allowBackup="false" plus
		data_extraction_rules.xml: it closes the "someone has the phone" path
		rather than the "someone has the backup" path.

		The app does no background work (no background fetch, no background
		URLSession, no notifications), so nothing needs to read the container
		while locked.

		REQUIRES the "Data Protection" capability on the App ID in the Apple
		Developer portal (Complete Protection). Without it, signing fails with a
		provisioning-profile mismatch. That step is in
		docs/kiro/NATIVE_RELEASE_GUIDE.md. Simulator builds with
		CODE_SIGNING_ALLOWED=NO ignore entitlements entirely, so CI does not
		prove this; on-device behaviour is a DEVICE GATE.
	-->
	<key>com.apple.developer.default-data-protection</key>
	<string>NSFileProtectionComplete</string>

	<!--
		DELIBERATELY ABSENT ENTITLEMENTS

		com.apple.developer.applesignin
			`signInWithApple()` (src/lib/supabase.ts) calls
			`startOAuth('apple')`, the same Supabase web OAuth path as Google:
			the system browser opens the provider and returns through
			gomsinlog://auth/callback. Nothing calls
			ASAuthorizationAppleIDProvider, so the entitlement is not required,
			and claiming it would make signing fail on any profile that has not
			enabled the capability. If a future version adopts the native
			Sign in with Apple sheet, add the capability AND this entitlement
			together.

		keychain-access-groups
			The app never touches the Keychain. See the Keychain section of
			docs/kiro/NATIVE_RELEASE_GUIDE.md. Declaring a shared access group
			would create a way for another bundle to read whatever ended up
			there.

		com.apple.developer.associated-domains
			Deep linking uses the custom `gomsinlog` scheme, not Universal
			Links, so there is no domain to associate and no
			apple-app-site-association file to host.

		com.apple.developer.icloud-container-identifiers / ubiquity-*
			No iCloud storage. Sync is Supabase only.

		aps-environment
			No push notifications in v1.
	-->
</dict>
</plist>
